From d4272c39801167d2b63a2d770bfaaf2aae9428df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:44:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] tests: session-context reset waits for an import in
 flight on another thread

tests/hermes_state/test_storage_health_latch.py::test_readiness_probe_latches_a_file_that_is_not_a_database
errored at setup on CI (run 43407551871, passed on retry):

  AttributeError: partially initialized module 'gateway.session_context' has no
  attribute 'reset_session_vars' (most likely due to a circular import)

Not CPU starvation. Why:
1. The autouse _reset_session_context_vars fixture read sys.modules directly and
   called reset_session_vars() on whatever module object it found.
2. sys.modules holds a module before its body has run while another thread is
   importing it.
3. Another thread was: the previous test latched the canonical state.db, and
   note_storage_error -> schedule_incident starts a daemon "state-db-incident"
   thread that imports gateway.status / hermes_cli.kanban_db (transitively
   gateway.session_context) to file a Kanban incident card.
4. That thread outlives the test, so the next test's setup races its imports.

Fix:
- tests/_fixtures/session_context_reset.py: when the module is in sys.modules,
  get it via importlib.import_module, which waits on the module's import lock
  until an in-flight import finishes. Covers any leaked thread, not just this one.
- test_storage_health_latch.py: stub schedule_incident in the autouse fixture
  (as test_storage_corruption_incident.py does), so these latch tests no longer
  leak incident-reporter threads writing cards into a torn-down HERMES_HOME.

Proof:
- Deterministic repro: a meta_path loader holding gateway.session_context
  mid-exec in the incident thread reproduced the exact CI error on main
  (6 passed, 2 errors); with the fixture fix 8 passed.
- New tests/test_conftest_session_context_reset.py holds a probe module's import
  open on one thread and resets from another: red on the old fixture (the same
  "partially initialized module" AttributeError), green with the fix.
- Thread probe: after the fix no state-db-incident thread is alive at any setup
  in test_storage_health_latch.py (before: 1, then 2).
- scripts/run_tests.sh on the new test, test_storage_health_latch,
  test_storage_corruption_incident, test_conftest_state_monkeypatch: 24 passed.
